CurlFtpFS
=========

The repository currently contains **two tracks**:

1. **Legacy, complete FTP filesystem implementation in C** (the real mount functionality).
2. **In-progress Rust port** focused on LIST parsing.

Where is the ftpfs functionality?
=================================

The actual FUSE FTP filesystem behavior (mounting, read/write, reconnect logic, cache integration,
libcurl interaction) is still implemented in the legacy C sources, primarily:

- `ftpfs.c`
- `cache.c`
- `path_utils.c`
- `charset_utils.c`

The Rust code added so far does **not** yet implement end-to-end mounting. It currently ports
only directory-list parsing to make iterative migration/test-driven porting possible.

Rust components currently available
===================================

- `src/parser.rs`: UNIX/Windows FTP LIST parsing.
- `src/cache.rs`: Rust cache behavior/TTL invalidation and cache option parsing.
- `src/path_utils.rs`: path assembly helpers ported from C path utilities.
- `src/charset_utils.rs`: charset conversion API surface (UTF-8 identity + explicit unsupported errors).
- `src/main.rs`: simple parser inspection CLI.
- `tests/parser.rs`, `tests/cache_path.rs`: regression tests.

Build and test Rust parser
==========================

```bash
cargo build
cargo test
```

Legacy C implementation
=======================

For full ftpfs behavior today, continue using/building the legacy C implementation in this repo.
